+For the existing URL-supervised command, the attended view SHALL identify the run and attempt and show the observed step, original deadline, limit status and next permissible action in its first state cue. Status, reason and action SHALL remain available as plain text. Only current evidence from the trusted supervisor for that run and attempt may establish a live or terminal state. The view SHALL preserve the established bounded state read and show Unknown with a safe reason and recovery help when the relevant observation is missing, stale, inconsistent or bound to another run or attempt. A saved record, an attached view or a completed input check alone SHALL NOT establish live progress, offline completion or cleanup.
+
+A verified detach from the live attempt SHALL show the observed start of one detached interval, the original deadline for that attempt and the existing attach action. A verified return to the same live attempt SHALL show the corresponding observed end once. Repeated attachment SHALL retain that interval without launching a child, repeating a stop, replaying input or advancing a step. An unavailable or unverified endpoint remains Unknown. A stopped, expired or unverified attempt SHALL NOT appear live on return. Show stopping while cleanup is unverified and state the outstanding check. The view MAY show the existing resume action only when cleanup and stopped eligibility are verified under the existing resume rules. Inspecting retained state does not itself resume work, prove cleanup or alter the deadline, pin, provider, policies, permissions or frozen subjects.
+
+The first wait cue SHALL distinguish an ordinary system wait, an eligible question awaiting operator action and an unavailable observation. For an eligible question, it SHALL name the Author pane and keep the wait visible without color. Where an interactive view and keyboard binding are available, it SHALL identify the action through the configured view or its keyboard-reachable help. With no such view or binding, plain text SHALL retain the eligible operator question and its Author role, say why keyboard focus is unavailable and give the available bounded recovery help. It SHALL NOT show an unavailable path or assert a focus or input effect. The view SHALL expose only admitted progress metadata and the permitted author-question cue. Focus and view attachment SHALL NOT deliver input to a role. An answer still requires the existing checked typed clarification route; arbitrary terminal input and helper role input remain refused. No source, role transcript or authentication bytes are authorized for display by the attended view.
+
